# Store every text file with LF line endings, whatever machine commits it.
#
# Until this file existed, only a global core.autocrlf=true on the Windows
# machine kept CRLF out of the repo - and Python's Path.write_text writes CRLF
# on Windows, so a script run locally produced it. A session on another machine
# or a phone, or a fresh clone without that setting, would have committed a
# whole-file line-ending diff of funds.json. This makes the repository
# enforce it rather than one machine's config.
#
# Working copies are unchanged: Windows checkouts still follow core.autocrlf.
* text=auto
